# HDFC SKY Terminal — House Rules

This is a widget-driven web trading terminal for HDFC SKY. The UI replicates the
Figma file `Terminal_testing` (key `aBbKoxTExS6gt1ZTMYr42B`) 1:1 in production React.

Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack) · React 19 · TypeScript · Tailwind v4.
Design system: HDFC SKY DS, in `design-system/hdfc-sky-design-system/`.

## Source of truth
- `widgets/_registry.ts` = available widgets. `screens/_registry.ts` = screen
  composition. NEVER bypass the registries by hand-editing layout/page files.
- The `.skills/*.md` files carry the full conventions. See @skills-index below.

## Colors
- One accent only: SKY blue `#2850E7` = `var(--accent)`. No teals/oranges/purples.
- Green = up, red = down. No exceptions. `var(--profit)` / `var(--loss)`. Never decorative.
- Cards are flat: `var(--bg-card)`, 1px `var(--border-1)`, 8px radius, NO shadow.
  Shadows only on modals (`var(--shadow-md)`) and popovers (`var(--shadow-pop)`).
- Tag fills are washed-out tints (e.g. `var(--sky-loss-bg)`), never saturated.

## Code
- CSS variables only — NEVER raw hex, never `text-gray-500`. See `app/globals.css`.
- Tailwind is for LAYOUT utilities only (flex, grid, gap, spacing). Not colors/fonts.
- Inline styles are fine inside widget innards (matches the Figma JSX). Don't convert
  to Tailwind without a reason.
- Theme-aware via CSS vars — they flip on `data-theme="dark"`. Don't branch on
  `useTheme()` unless you genuinely need theme-conditional logic.

## Type & numbers
- One family: Inter (self-hosted). Dense sizing: 10/11/12/14px dominate; 18/24/28 for headers.
- ALL numerics get `className="num"` (tabular figures so columns align).
- Indian numbering: `1,44,000.00`, `14,34,535.75`. Never `144,000`.
- `₹` symbol, no space for compact labels (`₹1.2L`). Change indicators paired:
  `-30.55 (-0.12%)`.

## Voice
- Operator's voice: calm, terse, no marketing fluff.
- No emoji. Ever. No exclamation marks.
- Title Case for buttons/tabs. ALL CAPS for status chips (`EXPIRY TODAY`, `STRIKE`).

## Workflow discipline
- One change at a time. Don't bundle unrelated edits.
- Don't import one widget into another — extract shared UI to `components/`.
- Mock data lives in each widget's `hooks.ts`. Don't wire real data in this loop.
- After any visual change: screenshot http://localhost:3000 and diff vs the Figma frame.
